Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Keeps VirtualDJ's full-screen mode on the screen it was already on,
; instead of jumping to the external TV.
;
; The window control in the header cycles windowed -> maximized ->
; full screen. On the last step VirtualDJ does everything right: it calls
; MonitorFromWindow, gets the laptop panel, and asks for that monitor's
; rect. Wine also does the right thing -- it sets _NET_WM_STATE_FULLSCREEN
; and then names the target output for the WM in _NET_WM_FULLSCREEN_MONITORS,
; using Xinerama monitor indices (0 = eDP-1, the laptop).
;
; mutter is what gets it wrong. meta_x11_display_ensure_xinerama_indices()
; matches XineramaQueryScreens() rects against its own logical monitor
; rects by *exact equality*. Both screens here run at scale 2, so mutter's
; logical rects (eDP-1 0,0 1920x1200; HDMI-2 1920,0 2048x1080) can never
; equal XWayland's device-pixel Xinerama rects (0,0 3840x2400 and
; 3840,0 4096x2160). No logical monitor is ever assigned an index, so they
; all keep the g_new0 default of 0, and index 0 resolves to whichever
; monitor is *first* in the list -- which in this layout is the TV.
; (Wine then observes the move and re-sends index 1, which matches nothing,
; so mutter clears the property entirely. That is why a full-screen
; VirtualDJ window has no _NET_WM_FULLSCREEN_MONITORS on it at all.)
; This is an upstream mutter bug, still present in main; it needs both
; HiDPI scaling and two monitors to show up.
;
; UseXRandR=N is the lever that avoids it without patching anything.
; It makes X11DRV_XRandR_Init() bail out early, so Wine keeps the
; "Xinerama" display-device handler (priority 100) that xinerama_init()
; already registered instead of "XRandR 1.4" (priority 200). That handler
; still enumerates BOTH monitors correctly -- it reads the same
; XineramaQueryScreens data -- but its register_event_handlers is NULL, so
; X11DRV_DisplayDevices_SupportEventHandlers() returns FALSE and
; update_net_wm_fullscreen_monitors() returns before sending anything.
; With no index for mutter to mistranslate, mutter picks the full-screen
; output from the window's actual geometry: the laptop when it is on the
; laptop, and the TV if the window is moved there first.
;
; Two things are given up, neither of which VirtualDJ uses:
;   - Display hotplug detection. Wine no longer receives XRandR events, so
;     plugging or unplugging the TV mid-session is not noticed until
;     VirtualDJ restarts.
;   - Mode setting. Display settings fall back to NoRes/XF86VidMode, so
;     ChangeDisplaySettings cannot change resolution. VirtualDJ uses
;     windowed full screen, not an exclusive mode, so this does not bite.
;
; Verified 2026-09-09: with this set, the trace shows
;   requesting _NET_WM_STATE 0x2
;   requesting config (0,0)-(3840,2400)
; and no _NET_WM_FULLSCREEN_MONITORS at all, and the window goes full
; screen on the laptop across repeated cycles.
;
; Do NOT try to fix this by switching Wine to winewayland.drv
; (HKCU\Software\Wine\Drivers "Graphics"="wayland"). It does remove the
; faulty path -- the Wayland driver names outputs by connector, so there is
; no index to mistranslate -- and the UI renders at the correct size, but
; VirtualDJ livelocks within a minute: the main thread keeps wined3d's
; command-stream critical section while mutter re-sends
; xdg_toplevel_handle_configure with climbing serials, and the UI stops
; responding at ~80% CPU ("wait timed out in thread NNNN, blocked by NNNN"
; against dlls/wined3d/wined3d_main.c: wined3d_cs). Tested 2026-09-09 on
; wine 11.17.
[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Wine\X11 Driver]
"UseXRandR"="N"
